From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:00:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: Codex installs with its own installer; an update is
 offered only when it can run

Codex was installed with `npm install -g` through whatever npm the machine
had, and the Update button was always shown. A machine without Node could
not install it at all, and an installation npm had no right to replace
failed with EACCES.

Install now runs Codex's own installer without questions, as Codex's own
updater does. The Update button follows the way `codex update` would run:
Codex's own installation, a global npm folder this user can write to, or
Homebrew on macOS. Otherwise no update is offered. An install on a host
without curl says so instead of starting.
